1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,667
Hi, I am Divij Pawar, and this

2
00:00:01,667 --> 00:00:03,333
video is about what happens when two

3
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:05,542
AI agents disagree and a person has

4
00:00:05,542 --> 00:00:06,625
to decide between them.

5
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:09,208
The narration you're hearing is AI generated,

6
00:00:09,417 --> 00:00:10,875
but the work it describes is mine.

7
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:12,708
This run asked two agents when the

8
00:00:12,708 --> 00:00:15,125
first Pokémon game reached North America, and

9
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:17,000
one of them said nineteen ninety-eight while

10
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,875
the other said nineteen ninety-six.

11
00:00:18,917 --> 00:00:20,750
The system flagged the disagreement and then

12
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:22,958
stopped, and it has been waiting for

13
00:00:22,958 --> 00:00:24,875
a person to decide ever since.

14
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:27,245
Part one made the comparison between the

15
00:00:27,245 --> 00:00:29,287
two agents stricter, so that figures are

16
00:00:29,287 --> 00:00:31,328
now compared by metric, period, unit, and

17
00:00:31,328 --> 00:00:31,828
source.

18
00:00:32,203 --> 00:00:33,620
This part is about what happens when

19
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:35,537
that comparison finds a real disagreement,

20
00:00:35,745 --> 00:00:37,662
because flagging a contradiction is only useful

21
00:00:37,662 --> 00:00:39,162
if something actually happens next.

22
00:00:39,662 --> 00:00:40,828
A gate like this needs a trigger

23
00:00:40,828 --> 00:00:42,620
you can test, a stop that actually

24
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:44,495
holds, a named person who gives a

25
00:00:44,495 --> 00:00:46,453
written reason, and a record nobody can

26
00:00:46,453 --> 00:00:48,870
edit, and without all four it's really

27
00:00:48,870 --> 00:00:49,703
just a warning.

28
00:00:50,470 --> 00:00:52,303
The trigger is deliberately narrow, so a

29
00:00:52,303 --> 00:00:53,970
run only waits when two agents cite

30
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:55,803
different values for the same figure and

31
00:00:55,845 --> 00:00:57,637
the same period, while a figure that

32
00:00:57,637 --> 00:00:59,303
only one agent mentions is shown for

33
00:00:59,303 --> 00:01:01,303
review without stopping anything, because there's

34
00:01:01,303 --> 00:01:02,428
nothing to decide between.

35
00:01:03,220 --> 00:01:05,012
Runs stored before the gate existed are

36
00:01:05,012 --> 00:01:07,053
never gated after the fact, since changing

37
00:01:07,053 --> 00:01:08,512
the rules on old records is how

38
00:01:08,512 --> 00:01:10,720
audit trails get rewritten, and in practice

39
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:12,470
most runs never reach the gate at

40
00:01:12,470 --> 00:01:12,970
all.

41
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,883
The decision form opens in the same

42
00:01:14,883 --> 00:01:16,675
place you're already reading, so it never

43
00:01:16,675 --> 00:01:17,633
covers the evidence.

44
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:19,925
The reviewer picks one of five outcomes,

45
00:01:19,925 --> 00:01:21,300
which are that agent A is right,

46
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:23,008
that agent B is right, that both

47
00:01:23,008 --> 00:01:24,883
are wrong, that there's no real conflict,

48
00:01:24,883 --> 00:01:26,467
or that the correct value is something

49
00:01:26,467 --> 00:01:28,258
they enter themselves, and then they have

50
00:01:28,258 --> 00:01:29,383
to give their reasoning in at least

51
00:01:29,550 --> 00:01:31,467
twenty characters, which is deliberately too

52
00:01:31,467 --> 00:01:33,300
long for something like looks good, before

53
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:34,092
typing their name.

54
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:36,117
The small print under the name field

55
00:01:36,117 --> 00:01:37,867
says that it's recorded as entered and

56
00:01:37,867 --> 00:01:40,242
not verified, because the login only carries

57
00:01:40,242 --> 00:01:41,783
a permission level and not an actual

58
00:01:41,783 --> 00:01:43,700
person, and the screen says that every

59
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:44,200
time.

60
00:01:44,783 --> 00:01:45,992
If a decision breaks one of the

61
00:01:45,992 --> 00:01:47,783
rules, it's refused and the reason is

62
00:01:47,783 --> 00:01:49,908
explained in words, so a decision about

63
00:01:49,908 --> 00:01:52,200
a figure that nobody disputed is turned

64
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,992
away rather than quietly fixed.

65
00:01:54,580 --> 00:01:56,413
A later decision can supersede an earlier

66
00:01:56,413 --> 00:01:58,122
one, but both stay on the record,

67
00:01:58,122 --> 00:02:00,663
because the database itself blocks edits and

68
00:02:00,663 --> 00:02:01,205
deletions.

69
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:03,398
While a run is waiting, an investor

70
00:02:03,398 --> 00:02:05,148
sees the figures the agents agreed on

71
00:02:05,148 --> 00:02:06,898
along with a notice, and the server

72
00:02:06,898 --> 00:02:09,232
withholds the disputed values and both agents'

73
00:02:09,357 --> 00:02:09,857
answers.

74
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:11,857
When I searched the investor's view of

75
00:02:11,857 --> 00:02:13,857
this run, nineteen ninety-six never appeared,

76
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:16,107
but nineteen ninety-eight appeared once, inside

77
00:02:16,107 --> 00:02:17,648
a search result shown in the run's

78
00:02:17,648 --> 00:02:19,565
trace, so the trace now withholds what

79
00:02:19,565 --> 00:02:21,190
each search returned while the gate is

80
00:02:21,190 --> 00:02:23,232
open, and after that fix the same

81
00:02:23,232 --> 00:02:24,523
search finds neither year.

82
00:02:25,065 --> 00:02:27,315
The withholding still depends on read access,

83
00:02:27,315 --> 00:02:29,357
because a request without a token is

84
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:30,857
served at the level the run was

85
00:02:30,857 --> 00:02:31,440
stored with.

86
00:02:32,170 --> 00:02:33,962
Nobody has recorded a decision on that

87
00:02:33,962 --> 00:02:35,587
run yet, so it is still open,

88
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,587
which is exactly how the gate is

89
00:02:37,587 --> 00:02:39,378
meant to behave until a person looks

90
00:02:39,378 --> 00:02:39,878
at it.

91
00:02:40,510 --> 00:02:41,927
Two agents can agree with each other

92
00:02:41,927 --> 00:02:43,760
and still both be wrong, so each

93
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,843
agent's figures are also checked against accounting

94
00:02:45,843 --> 00:02:48,218
identities, such as basic earnings per share

95
00:02:48,218 --> 00:02:50,302
never being lower than diluted, free cash

96
00:02:50,302 --> 00:02:52,718
flow equalling operating cash flow minus capital

97
00:02:52,718 --> 00:02:55,052
spending, and assets equalling liabilities

98
00:02:55,052 --> 00:02:55,802
plus equity.

99
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:58,052
When an agent's figures break one of

100
00:02:58,052 --> 00:02:59,718
those, the run waits for a person

101
00:02:59,718 --> 00:03:01,177
just as it does for a mismatch,

102
00:03:01,677 --> 00:03:03,552
and the reviewer can confirm the error

103
00:03:03,552 --> 00:03:04,968
instead of picking an agent.

104
00:03:05,770 --> 00:03:07,437
Every figure an agent cites is also

105
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:09,062
checked against the filing it was given,

106
00:03:09,395 --> 00:03:10,687
and rounding to the number of digits

107
00:03:10,687 --> 00:03:11,978
the agent wrote is allowed.

108
00:03:12,562 --> 00:03:14,603
In one Microsoft run, an agent was

109
00:03:14,603 --> 00:03:16,645
given revenue of eighty-two point nine billion

110
00:03:16,645 --> 00:03:18,228
and wrote eight hundred twenty-eight point

111
00:03:18,228 --> 00:03:18,937
nine billion.

112
00:03:19,312 --> 00:03:21,270
That attempt failed its format check first,

113
00:03:21,437 --> 00:03:23,145
so this check never actually ran on

114
00:03:23,145 --> 00:03:24,103
it, but it would have caught the

115
00:03:24,103 --> 00:03:24,978
mistake if it had.

116
00:03:25,590 --> 00:03:27,507
Other rules only describe what is usually

117
00:03:27,507 --> 00:03:28,007
true.

118
00:03:28,382 --> 00:03:30,090
On one Google run, net income came

119
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:32,048
out at nearly three times operating income,

120
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:33,715
and the filing showed the same thing,

121
00:03:33,715 --> 00:03:35,715
because it reflected a real one-off gain.

122
00:03:36,173 --> 00:03:37,632
That's why rules like this never stop

123
00:03:37,632 --> 00:03:38,965
a run and only mark the result

124
00:03:38,965 --> 00:03:40,340
as unusual and worth a look.

125
00:03:40,882 --> 00:03:43,048
The same finding also explained two figures

126
00:03:43,048 --> 00:03:45,340
that part one had left unrecognised, which

127
00:03:45,340 --> 00:03:46,965
turned out to be Google's filed earnings

128
00:03:46,965 --> 00:03:47,507
per share.

129
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:49,807
The filing itself goes through the same

130
00:03:49,807 --> 00:03:51,598
checks, using the single fetch that has

131
00:03:51,598 --> 00:03:53,682
already been made, and Apple's balance sheet

132
00:03:53,682 --> 00:03:54,182
adds up.

133
00:03:54,932 --> 00:03:56,182
In the middle of this testing, though,

134
00:03:56,348 --> 00:03:58,473
the local model stopped responding, to the

135
00:03:58,473 --> 00:04:00,515
point where a five-token test request got

136
00:04:00,515 --> 00:04:03,015
no reply within sixty seconds, and because

137
00:04:03,015 --> 00:04:05,223
model calls have no timeout, a stuck

138
00:04:05,223 --> 00:04:07,598
model can hold up a comparison indefinitely.

139
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,823
Every figure the agents were given can

140
00:04:09,823 --> 00:04:11,448
now be found in the original filing,

141
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:13,615
because the system opens the actual SEC

142
00:04:13,615 --> 00:04:16,157
document, finds the exact tagged value, and

143
00:04:16,157 --> 00:04:17,823
returns the row, the column, and the

144
00:04:17,823 --> 00:04:18,782
number as it was filed.

145
00:04:19,490 --> 00:04:20,782
In the last batch it found all

146
00:04:21,032 --> 00:04:23,240
twenty-four figures and every filed value matched,

147
00:04:23,490 --> 00:04:24,823
and in the review each figure now

148
00:04:24,823 --> 00:04:26,365
has a source button that opens that

149
00:04:26,365 --> 00:04:28,573
excerpt in place, while web figures show

150
00:04:28,573 --> 00:04:30,365
the snippet the agent actually read.

151
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:32,585
You can also watch a comparison as

152
00:04:32,585 --> 00:04:33,085
it happens.

153
00:04:33,502 --> 00:04:35,293
Each agent has its own lane showing

154
00:04:35,293 --> 00:04:36,960
what it's doing at that moment, and

155
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:39,210
the single shared SEC fetch is drawn

156
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:41,293
only once, because it only happened once.

157
00:04:41,918 --> 00:04:43,752
Every indicator on that screen comes from

158
00:04:43,752 --> 00:04:44,835
a real server event.

159
00:04:45,510 --> 00:04:47,343
Analysts don't stop at the figures, because

160
00:04:47,343 --> 00:04:48,718
they also make a call, so after

161
00:04:48,718 --> 00:04:50,760
each answer passes its checks, a second

162
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:52,260
call to the same model reads that

163
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,343
answer and extracts a grade, a direction,

164
00:04:54,510 --> 00:04:56,093
the stated assumptions, and up to three

165
00:04:56,093 --> 00:04:58,260
key points, all labelled as model judgment.

166
00:04:58,968 --> 00:05:00,385
Anything it quotes that isn't in the

167
00:05:00,385 --> 00:05:02,552
agent's own answer or inputs is dropped,

168
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,427
and when the extraction fails, the run

169
00:05:04,427 --> 00:05:05,635
carries on and says so.

170
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:08,020
When two grades differ, the system works

171
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:09,812
out whether the agents used different figures

172
00:05:09,812 --> 00:05:11,978
or periods, used the same figures with

173
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:13,770
different assumptions, or differed on neither,

174
00:05:14,062 --> 00:05:15,270
in which case it comes down to

175
00:05:15,270 --> 00:05:16,562
how they weighed the same evidence.

176
00:05:17,437 --> 00:05:19,187
A consensus is only recorded when both

177
00:05:19,187 --> 00:05:20,728
the grade and the direction agree and

178
00:05:20,728 --> 00:05:22,603
no hard rule has failed, and anything

179
00:05:22,603 --> 00:05:24,062
else goes to the gate, where the

180
00:05:24,062 --> 00:05:26,020
reviewer can accept one agent's grade or

181
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:28,770
set the grade themselves, while investors see

182
00:05:28,770 --> 00:05:30,853
no grade until a person has recorded

183
00:05:30,853 --> 00:05:31,353
one.

184
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:33,252
The review now reads in the order

185
00:05:33,252 --> 00:05:35,002
a person needs it, starting with the

186
00:05:35,002 --> 00:05:36,835
answer and whether anything failed a check,

187
00:05:36,835 --> 00:05:38,918
followed by the decision, then the evidence

188
00:05:38,918 --> 00:05:41,085
figure by figure, then the agents, and

189
00:05:41,085 --> 00:05:43,293
finally the underlying machinery, which is

190
00:05:43,293 --> 00:05:43,960
folded away.

191
00:05:44,710 --> 00:05:46,668
Every review can also be exported as

192
00:05:46,668 --> 00:05:47,502
a plain document.

193
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:50,023
Several things work now that didn't before.

194
00:05:50,648 --> 00:05:52,440
A mismatch, a failed hard check, or

195
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,190
a grade disagreement stops the run until

196
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:56,273
a person decides, decisions need a reason

197
00:05:56,273 --> 00:05:58,273
and can't be edited, and investors don't

198
00:05:58,273 --> 00:06:00,482
receive the disputed values, either agent's

199
00:06:00,482 --> 00:06:02,398
answer, or anything the searches returned.

200
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:04,982
Accounting rules check each agent and the

201
00:06:04,982 --> 00:06:07,065
filing, and every review can be exported

202
00:06:07,065 --> 00:06:08,107
as a plain document.

203
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:09,987
Some things still don't work.

204
00:06:10,195 --> 00:06:11,778
The decider's name is typed in and

205
00:06:11,778 --> 00:06:13,862
never verified, and anyone can create a

206
00:06:13,862 --> 00:06:15,820
reviewer token, which is a known security

207
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:16,320
gap.

208
00:06:16,862 --> 00:06:18,737
The storage still holds everything and the

209
00:06:18,737 --> 00:06:20,570
withholding only happens when the data is

210
00:06:20,570 --> 00:06:22,737
read, the grade extraction is the same

211
00:06:22,737 --> 00:06:24,903
model judging its own answer, and model

212
00:06:24,903 --> 00:06:26,028
calls still have no timeout.

213
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:28,857
The judgment stays with a person, and

214
00:06:28,857 --> 00:06:30,107
this is the first time the system

215
00:06:30,107 --> 00:06:31,482
can't move forward without one.

216
00:06:32,065 --> 00:06:33,398
The smallest true claim I can make

217
00:06:33,398 --> 00:06:35,398
is that the machine fetches, reads, compares,

218
00:06:35,690 --> 00:06:37,023
checks and grades, and then it stops

219
00:06:37,023 --> 00:06:37,523
and waits.

220
00:06:37,982 --> 00:06:39,440
If you run agents yourself, take one

221
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,023
warning your system raises, give it a

222
00:06:41,023 --> 00:06:42,523
trigger, a stop, a person, and a

223
00:06:42,523 --> 00:06:44,065
record, and then check that it can't

224
00:06:44,065 --> 00:06:44,648
clear itself.

225
00:06:44,982 --> 00:06:46,398
For now, this one run is still

226
00:06:46,398 --> 00:06:46,898
open.

227
00:06:47,410 --> 00:06:49,952
One run, still open, written down, versioned,

228
00:06:49,952 --> 00:06:50,702
and executable.

229
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:51,660
Signing off, Divij Pawar.
